Version 0.1  2026-08-19 (first release)
	Convert images to SIXEL and write them to the terminal
	Add the imcat command line tool, with --max-height/--max-width
	  subsampling limits and --version
	Add a matplotlib backend (syxel.backend_sixel), scaling figures to
	  the terminal and registering a sixel savefig format
	Quantize to at most 256 colour registers, falling back to a fixed
	  5x9x5 RGB cube when the most frequent colours do not cover the image
	Run-length encode the output
	Report image files that cannot be read (missing, unreadable, or not
	  an image) as an error message rather than a traceback, skipping
	  them and exiting with a non-zero status
	Make imread (imcat extra) and matplotlib (matplotlib extra) optional;
	  numpy is the only hard dependency
